  "brief": "DoorDash is acquiring Instacart in a $17 billion deal pending antitrust review, aiming to expand its grocery delivery business.\n\nDoorDash / Instacart (Pending approval): DoorDash to Buy Instacart. DoorDash is acquiring Instacart in a $17 billion deal [1, 2, 3]. The deal is pending antitrust review [4, 5, 6]. The acquisition aims to expand DoorDash's grocery delivery business [7, 8].\nThrive Holdings / ADT (Announced): Thrive Holdings to Acquire ADT. Thrive Holdings is acquiring ADT for $7.6 billion [16, 18, 19]. The deal was announced on October 29th [14, 15, 20]. The acquisition is an all-cash deal [16, 18, 19].\nBASF / Evonik (Rumored): BASF and Evonik Takeover Rumors. BASF is trying to acquire Evonik, but Evonik is likely to reject the offer [21, 22, 24]. BASF has increased its bid to €24 per share, but Evonik has rejected the offer [25, 26]. BASF is stepping up its push for Evonik after the initial offer was rejected [23].\nSalesforce / Rune Technologies (Announced): Salesforce to Acquire Rune Technologies. Salesforce has agreed to acquire Rune Technologies in its most significant defense acquisition to date [28, 27]. The deal is expected to be completed in the first half of 2024 [28]. No further details on the deal have been disclosed [28].\nCD&R / Global Payments (Announced): CD&R and Global Payments Deal. CD&R is pursuing a buyout of Global Payments [33, 36]. The deal was announced [33]. The next step is unclear [33, 36].\nAIG / Everest's Chile business (Completed): AIG to Acquire Everest's Chile Business. AIG is acquiring Everest's Chile business as part of its expansion into Latin America [37]. The deal completes AIG's acquisition of Everest's Colombian business [37].\nLuda Technology Group / AI Data Quant Tech (Announced): Luda Technology Group to Acquire AI Data Quant Tech Stake. Luda Technology Group is acquiring a 55% stake in AI Data Quant Tech [38]. The deal was announced by Luda Technology Group [38].\nPateno Payments Inc. / XTM Inc.'s EveryDay Platform (Completed): Pateno Payments Inc. Acquires XTM Inc.'s EveryDay Platform. Pateno Payments Inc. has acquired the EveryDay Platform from XTM Inc [39]. The acquisition is completed and the deal is now closed [39].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- LCI Board Reiterates Support for Merger with Patrick [41].\n- Dark Matter acquires House Numbers’ agentic AI platform [43].\n- LCI rejects $101-per-share takeover offer, sticks with Patrick merger [47].",
